<card id="c" title="Zla Kolata and Prokletije: 300 Euros There and Back">
<do type="prev" label="Back"><prev/></do>
<p>I didn&apos;t look at specific trails. I just found a campsite with meals and a stunning view of the mountains and decided I&apos;d stay there and figure out where to go once I got there.</p>
<p>I bought the bus tickets, booked the campsite and waited for my vacation.</p>
<p>Not researching the trails in advance turned out to be a mistake. But more on that later.</p>
<p><b>2. The bus</b></p>
<p>Vacation finally started. The trip began in Belgrade, and the first obstacle was waiting for me right there, at the main bus station.</p>
<p>I got there forty minutes before departure and went to figure out how to get onto the platform, and which one.</p>
<p>To get onto the platforms at Belgrade&apos;s main bus station, you need a separate ticket. I knew that. What I didn&apos;t expect was having to buy it at the ticket office, after standing in a line of twenty-plus people.</p>
